.TH WORDCOUNT 3 "September 2026" "libmyutils 1.0" "libmyutils Manual"
.SH NAME
wordCount \- count lines, words and characters in a file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "myfilefunctions.h"
.sp
.BI "int wordCount(FILE *" file ", int *" lines ", int *" words ", int *" chars ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B wordCount()
function reads the open file stream
.I file
from its current position to end-of-file, and counts the number of
lines, words and characters, storing the results in
.IR lines ,
.I words
and
.I chars
respectively.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 on success, or \-1 on failure (for example if any pointer argument is NULL).
